  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Transitive ({他動詞|たどうし}). Takes を particle: ～を{装|よそお}う.\n\nCONJUGATION: Godan verb (wa-row): {装|よそお}わない, {装|よそお}います, {装|よそお}って.\n\nNUANCE: For sense 1, {装|よそお}う implies deliberate pretense or putting on a facade. For sense 2, it has a more literary quality and is often used for formal or seasonal attire.\n\nNOMINAL FORM: {装|よそお}い (appearance, attire, decoration)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {平静|へいせい}を{装|よそお}う (to feign composure)\n- ～ふりを{装|よそお}う (to pretend to ~)\n- {身|み}を{装|よそお}う (to dress oneself)\n- {秋|あき}/{春|はる}の{装|よそお}い (autumn/spring attire)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {振|ふ}りをする (to pretend - more common)\n- {偽装|ぎそう}する (to disguise, falsify)\n- {着飾|きかざ}る (to dress up finely)",
